{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_79","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nAll five prior findings are fixed. Two additional medium blockers remain in Markdown association parsing.\n\nThe focused closeout-policy tests passed across domain, CLI, and MCP packages. The round-twelve and round-thirteen regressions also passed without skips. The worktree remains unchanged.\n\nPrior findings:\n\n| Finding | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| R11-N39 | fixed | `associationList` preserves presence and rejects empty items and duplicates; round-twelve regressions passed. |\n| R12-N42 | fixed | `approvedBeforeAdoption` checks the sealed plan; both history regressions passed. |\n| R12-N43 | fixed | Both templates declare `adrs: []`; template regression passed. |\n| R12-N44 | fixed | Fence character and length are preserved; longer-fence regression passed. |\n| R12-N45 | fixed | Keys are trimmed and values cleaned before duplicate detection; normalization regressions passed. |\n\nNew blockers:\n\n- **N46 — medium**, [closeout_adr_associations.go:92](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3650767735/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go:92): Code filtering can discard real association links. An indented code line containing `~~~` is treated as a fence opener and suppresses subsequent prose. Comment removal also crosses fenced-code boundaries.\n- **N47 — medium**, [closeout_adr_associations.go:33](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3650767735/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go:33): Balanced parentheses in a valid link destination truncate the parsed ADR filename. Both defects can incorrectly exempt a two-member roadmap under `when-justified`.\n\nRules applied: mixed Go feature and governance change; review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N46\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\",\n      \"line\": 92,\n      \"summary\": \"Preserve Markdown block context before excluding code and comments. TrimSpace makes a four-space-indented literal fence delimiter into an opening fenced block: the valid Markdown body '    ~~~\\\\n\\\\nGoverns [the pair](../roadmaps/pair.md).\\\\n' loses its real association link. Separately, line 75 removes comments before recognizing code: '~~~\\\\n<!--\\\\n~~~\\\\n\\\\n[real](../roadmaps/pair.md)\\\\n\\\\n<!-- -->\\\\n' loses the real link because the literal comment opener inside code consumes through the later comment. Read-only reproductions of the production filter logic confirmed both losses. With two canonical members and no other association, closeoutADRAssociations reports no diagnostic and the evaluator grants Known=true, Required=false, contrary to R3. Respect indented-code and fenced-code context, including comment precedence, and add evaluator regressions in both association directions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N47\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\",\n      \"line\": 33,\n      \"summary\": \"Parse balanced parentheses in inline Markdown destinations before resolving the association. The valid link '[decision](../adr/decision(extra).md)' to a regular canonical ADR file is matched as '../adr/decision(extra' by the production regex. The namespace filter then silently discards it because the truncated destination does not end in .md. I extracted and executed the exact production regex and confirmed that result. R3 permits basename .md ADR files without excluding parentheses and promises explicit local Markdown associations. A two-member roadmap whose sole association uses this link therefore receives an unjustified exemption. Parse the complete destination or return unknown for unsupported association syntax; cover forward and reverse links.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R11-N39\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go:115-155 preserves declaration presence, rejects duplicate normalized keys, missing values and empty list items. Ran go test ./internal/pose -run '^TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRound(Twelve|Thirteen)$' -count=1 -v; strict declaration regressions passed without skips.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N42\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go:699-760 requires enabled legacy-cutoff evidence or approvedBeforeAdoption, which rejects sealed plans carrying CloseoutReview. The post-adoption approval and disabled-policy regressions in TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundThirteen passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N43\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \".pose/templates/roadmap.md:6 and pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/.pose/templates/roadmap.md:6 declare adrs: []. associationList applies cleanValue to the adjacent comment. The distributed-template regression passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N44\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go:80-103 retains fence character and full length and requires a delimiter-only closing line of sufficient length. The longer-fence regression passed. N46 reports separate Markdown block-context defects.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N45\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go:127-135 trims keys, cleans values and detects differently spaced duplicates. TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundThirteen association normalization subtests all passed.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed R1-R7, decisions D1/D2, the accepted ADR, changed production code and tests, schema contracts, root/localized/scaffold docs, templates, applicable rules and relevant knowledge/debt records. Traced CLI close and receipt recovery/publication, closeout-check, review-check, review verification, review-plan, attention/obligations, reached, nextCloses, roadmap gates, dependency readiness, portfolio projection, MCP closeout state, federated acceptance and doctor. Examined never/always precedence, recorded-review vetoes, protected baseline and mandatory-human handling, canonical members/transfers, association resolution, historical sealed-plan distinction, receipt immutability and drift, schema adoption/downgrade paths and update compatibility. Ran the complete TestCloseoutReviewPolicy prefix across pose/cli/mcpserver successfully, then round-twelve/thirteen tests verbosely without skips. Ran artifact-check and surface-check; surface reported 213 results and zero findings. Artifact-check exited zero but displayed a recorded historical change set beyond the sealed head, so that display is not treated as proof of the sealed range's exact path count. An additional explicit-range artifact-check failed with a git broken-pipe error; a source CLI rerun could not build in the read-only temporary directory. Used sealed full-validation evidence and did not run writing assessments or record an attestation. Final git status --short was empty. Source-level reproductions established N46 and N47; no repository fixture was added.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Distinguished executable test results from implementer claims and source-level reproductions. Verified the five prior fixes. Full validation relies on sealed evidence; the artifact-check historical-range display and failed explicit-range attempt are disclosed. External writers ignoring governance locks remain outside the documented guarantee.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined guarded reevaluation, publication expectations, receipt ExpectAbsent behavior and intent/status/receipt recovery. Focused publication tests passed; no new asynchronous lifecycle was introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N47\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The declared local Markdown association contract silently loses a valid destination.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N46\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Association inputs can silently become absence rather than a resolved association or actionable unknown.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Traced shared evaluator and terminal projections through CLI, MCP, readiness, obligations and federation. The focused three-package integration prefix passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined receipt corruption/drift, unknown member and association diagnostics, incomplete close recovery and doctor remediation. Returned context identifies scope and required action; parser correctness exceptions are recorded separately.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N47\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Schema migration is explicit, but the new association reader does not honor 